data: {"type": "final", "payload": "核查结论：**该论断获得强支持**。文献库中检索到的证据一致支持\"RAG 能够降低大语言模型幻觉风险\"这一说法，未发现反驳或中立证据。\n\n## 核查结论\n\n**结论：RAG 降低 LLM 幻觉风险这一论断得到强支持。** 在核查到的 6 条证据中，全部为支持立场（置信度 0.9），无一条反驳或中立。\n\n**支持证据（代表性论文）**\n- 《Retrieval-Augmented Generation and Hallucination in Large Language Models: A Scholarly Overview》(2025) 明确指出 RAG 通过将模型输出\"接地\"（grounding）到外部知识来缓解幻觉。\n- 《Benchmarking Large Language Models in Retrieval-Augmented Generation》(2023) 将 RAG 描述为缓解 LLM 幻觉的\"有前景的方法\"。\n- 《MS-RAG: Simple and Effective Multi-Semantic Retrieval-Augmented Generation》(2025) 与《ReRag: A New Architecture for Reducing the Hallucination by Retrieval-Augmented Generation》(2024) 均以\"缓解幻觉\"作为 RAG 的核心动机。\n\n**审慎限定（重要）**\n需要指出的是，支持证据多来自论文的\"动机陈述\"层面——即 RAG 被提出和广泛采用正是为了缓解幻觉，这属于领域共识。但综述类文献（如《Hallucination Mitigation for Retrieval-Augmented Large Language Models: A Review》(2025)）同时提示：RAG 并非万能，检索到的内容本身可能错误或带偏（如检索谄媚、错误检索），反而会引入新的幻觉来源。因此更准确的表述是：**RAG 在\"正确检索到相关证据\"的前提下能显著降低幻觉，但其效果受检索质量制约**。\n\n综合来看，论断本身成立且证据充分，但应理解为\"有条件的强支持\"——RAG 是缓解幻觉的有效手段，而非彻底消除幻觉的保证。", "meta": {"runtime": "langgraph", "node": "reflect", "phase": "自检修正", "elapsed_ms": 650, "session_id": "t04-20260812T134352Z-run-1", "stop_reason": "completed", "tokens_in": 5887, "tokens_out": 389, "structured_answer": {"schema_version": "answer-contract/v1", "capability": "claim_verification", "status": "supported", "verdict_label": "强支持", "answer_mode": "evidence_based", "citation_compliance": "ok", "citations": [{"paper_id": "W4411065983", "title": "Retrieval-Augmented Generation and Hallucination in Large Language Models: A Scholarly Overview", "year": 2025, "chunk_uid": "85598e54abed9ffbc0fdb9a455d979f064cc365d", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) has emerged as a promising technique to mitigate hallucinations by grounding mo", "stance": "SUPPORT", "confidence": 0.9}, {"paper_id": "W4416035754", "title": "MS-RAG: Simple and Effective Multi-Semantic Retrieval-Augmented Generation", "year": 2025, "chunk_uid": "7a23375ff75a4c1cfa1b95bb4ed4218bc9134c1b", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "To alleviate the hallucination problem of large language model (LLM), retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) has been proposed and widely adopted.", "stance": "SUPPORT", "confidence": 0.9}, {"paper_id": "W4405272436", "title": "ReRag: A New Architecture for Reducing the Hallucination by Retrieval- Augmented Generation", "year": 2024, "chunk_uid": "d5ab39c21c6253bb31d68dc0d60ab2b9d753c40d", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "Recently, Retrieval-Augmented Generation systems (RAG) have been introduced to cope with this problem.", "stance": "SUPPORT", "confidence": 0.9}, {"paper_id": "2309.01431", "title": "Benchmarking Large Language Models in Retrieval-Augmented Generation", "year": 2023, "chunk_uid": "a36067aaf8a0b7b5f7075ba84805001d3ef35f51", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is a promising approach for mitigating the hallucination of large language models (LLMs).", "stance": "SUPPORT", "confidence": 0.9}], "uncertainty": {"category": "none", "message": "", "calibrated_rejection": false, "qualification_hints": []}, "tool_basis": ["verify_claim"], "claim": "检索增强生成(RAG)能够降低大语言模型回答中的幻觉风险"}}}

